ene line 'The mathematical statement ... is unconditional; only this physical identification ... invokes the conjecture', and the modular-double-vs-bar disambiguation. (2) UNDER-SPECIFIED CLAIM flagged by name in AGENTS.md: 'c_2 = -1 (bar-even) is Taylor-exact'. Per the 2026-08-16 ruling, 'Taylor' here is under-specified rather than false — c_2 = -1 IS the u^2 coefficient of the explicit-factor product prod_{k>=2}(1 + c_k u^k), but the full normalised model Phi(u)/Phi(0) has c-tilde_2 = c_2 - 1/8 = -9/8. The ruling's instruction is to say WHICH SERIES, never to delete the word. Proposed: 'c_2 = -1 (bar-even) is the exact u^2 coefficient of the explicit-factor product'. (3) CONVENTION LABEL MISSING: the owner ruling of 2026-08-15 makes convention D canonical and excises C, and the entire c_k ladder — c_2 = -1, c_3, and the cross-anchor swing — is convention-C-frame and has NOT been re-derived under D (bean qou-cds1). This block's '## Consequence for the c_k ladder' section states a general law (bar-parity predicts anchor-behaviour) from those rungs with no C-conditional label. Proposed: label the section C-conditional. SECONDARY, epistemic: 'This is confirmed on both available rungs' rests on n = 2, and one of the two is not independent evidence — c_2 = -1 is claimed structural (no fit, no CODATA, no q_0), so its anchor-stability follows by construction rather than confirming the parity law. The honest reading is one informative rung.","history":2},{"id":"trap-thesis-restatement","group":"trap","result":"pass","stale":true,"freshness":"stale","changed":["md","ts"],"at":"2026-08-21","reviewer":"agent","by":"agent:v03","history":2},{"id":"trap-triples","group":"trap","result":"pass","stale":true,"freshness":"stale","changed":["md","ts"],"at":"2026-08-21","reviewer":"agent","by":"agent:v03","history":2},{"id":"uses-editorial-hygiene","group":"uses","result":"pass","stale":true,"freshness":"stale","changed":["md","ts"],"at":"2026-08-09","reviewer":"script","by":"content/